<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="177" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Indexing recovers a document's parent record when the request has none, so documents moved by secure transitions (and Office/Compose saves) stay findable in record-scoped search and RAG (closes #1510)</title>
    <phase>Session 28 — UAC defect remediation (owner decision 2026-10-09: "fix now in uac-r2")</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Code change in the BFF indexing job; modifies tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A shared job handler used by several producers; the parent derivation must match Send-to-Index exactly.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits RagIndexingJobHandler and a shared parent-derivation helper; no file overlap with 175, 176 or 178.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, job, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 day</estimated-effort>
    <origin>#1510, confirmed by a probe test on master c8a87d818 (2026-10-09). uac-r2's own secure transitions (tasks 148/150/158/171) trigger it today: DocumentContainerRelocator calls RelocatedFileIndexing, which sends ParentEntity: null.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close #1510 (gh issue view 1510 has the evidence). When RagIndexingJobHandler receives a payload with no ParentEntity but a DocumentId, it derives the parent from the document row before indexing, so the new chunks carry parentEntityType and parentEntityId.</prompt>

  <goal>(1) Move RagEndpoints' Send-to-Index parent derivation (around :1255-1285; matter, project, invoice) into ONE shared helper. Extend it to the document's core-ancestor and regarding columns, so a document under a work assignment or event gets the right parent, named the way semantic search's scope=entity names parents.
(2) RagIndexingJobHandler uses the helper when payload.ParentEntity is null and DocumentId is set; it already injects IDocumentDataverseService. If the row cannot be read, index without a parent and log a warning, as today. Never fail the job over this, and never invent a parent.
(3) Send-to-Index uses the same helper, and its behaviour does not change.
(4) The producers this fixes are the relocator, UploadFinalizationWorker (Office new item), ComposeService create-on-save and AnalysisResultPersistence. Confirm each one passes DocumentId; where one doesn't but already has the id, make it pass it.</goal>

  <context>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/RelocatedFileIndexing.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/RagIndexingJobHandler.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/FileIndexingService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs (Send-to-Index derivation)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10/§11">Reuse before adding: one helper, justified in the notes. Measure the publish-size delta.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">No index schema change and no backfill job. Send-to-Index fixes existing chunks that have no parent; if a backfill is needed, propose it in the notes for the owner to decide.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Re-confirm the defect with the issue's Suspect 2 probe tests and keep them as regression tests.</step>
    <step>Add the shared helper, wire the job handler and Send-to-Index, and check each producer's DocumentId.</step>
    <step>Add the tests, write the notes and open the PR. If it is cheap, count read-only how many dev documents currently have no parent in the index, and report the number.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>The two #1510 probe tests pass, and the relocator test asserts that the job handler (not the enqueue) indexes the document with its parent.</criterion>
    <criterion>Parent derivation is tested for a matter, a project, a work assignment, an invoice, an unreadable row (no parent, and the job still succeeds) and a document with no parent link (no parent).</criterion>
    <criterion>Send-to-Index behaves exactly as before: its existing tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: the cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
